 ("Conflict", "Pumps.docx slide 1.114 says positive displacement pumps have 0% slip. The handbook p.22 and p.27 define slippage and show it in Figure 21. The lesson uses the handbook. Existing item Q345 does not state the 0% claim, so it is reused.", W(PU, "1.114 Knowledge Check PDP")),
 ("Conflict", "Slide 1.32 says total developed head is also referred to as shutoff head. The handbook p.14 defines shutoff head as the maximum head at a set speed. The lesson uses the handbook and leaves total developed head off.", W(PU, "1.32 Total Developed Head (TDH)")),
 ("Word claim", "Slide 1.20 says Psat is representative of NPSHR and that Psat increases as a discharge valve opens, and slide 1.24 ties temperature to NPSHR. The handbook p.12 to p.14 does not support this: NPSHR is a pump requirement set by testing, and Psat sits in NPSHA. Left off.", W(PU, "1.20 Net Positive Suction Head")),
 ("Word value", "Slide 1.35's worked answer states 4 = (33.9 + x - 50) - 0.8 and x = 21.1 feet. The arithmetic gives 20.9 feet. The marked choice, 21 feet, fits either. The question text is a picture, so the check is not used.", W(PU, "1.35 Knowledge Check Centrifugal Pump Terms- NPSH 2")),
 ("Word value", "Slide 1.36 marks 116 feet, but its explanation works out to 115 feet. The question text is a picture, so the check is not used.", W(PU, "1.36 Knowledge Check Centrifugal Pump Terms- Discharge Head")),
 ("Word claim", "Existing item Q342 follows slide 1.50, which gives low flow with low discharge pressure as the cavitation indication. The handbook p.12 and p.16 list noise and fluctuating pressure, flow, and motor current. Q342 is not reused here.", W(PU, "1.50 Knowledge Check Inidcations and Control of Pump Cavitation")),
 ("Word source", "Pump laws, system curves, operating point, and series and parallel operation on slides 1.67 to 1.85 have no ME-03 objective and are taught in HT-03. Pump efficiency, lift, jet pumps, and PDP NPSH on slides 1.28 to 1.33, 1.64 to 1.66, and 1.103 to 1.105 are left off. " + PICTURES, W(PU, "1.67 Centrifugal Pump Laws")),
 ("Word source", "ALIP Pumps.docx has no ME-03 objective, so it appears on a page marked From the lesson plan. Its slide 1.8 quiz says air gap power goes from the Outer Core/Stator to the Inner Core, while slide 1.4 says from the Stator to the Rotor, and sodium acts as the rotor. Air gap power and thrust are left off this page. Cards C214 to C217 already cover them.", S14),
 ("Scope", "Generic water in the handbook's pump text is untagged. Condensate depression on p.13, steam-driven direct-acting pumps on p.20 and p.21, and gland sealing water on slide 1.15 are left off. Most worked figures use water, so conversion values such as 0.433 from slide 1.21 are not shown.", 13),
 ("Handbook wording", "p.5 says the flow through a radial flow pump is shown for an axial pump. p.6 says mixed flow liquid goes to the pump suction, where discharge seems meant. The lesson does not repeat either. The handbook has no NPSH example, so the examples apply its equation to new numbers.", 5),
 ("Figures", "Figures 2, 4, 5, and 15 are off. They show detail that no objective needs.", 2),
